## Recommended next: Batch 21b — TenantXenditConfig CRUD + admin UI (T2 ~22-28K)

Wires up the existing-but-unused TenantXenditConfig schema model. Tenant Administrators
get a settings page to enter their Xendit credentials (secret key, public key, webhook
token, isLive flag, enabled methods array). Secret + token fields encrypted at rest via
21a's encrypt() before write; decrypt() called only at use-time in 21c. Test-connection
procedure creates a $0.01 placeholder invoice on Xendit's real API then voids it — proves
the credentials work AND flips isVerified to true.

Scope:
- NEW: `apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/admin-xendit-config.ts` — protected router with
  Tenant Administrator role check. Procedures:
    - `get` (query): returns current config WITHOUT decrypted secrets (only isLive,
      isVerified, enabledMethods, publicKey, updatedAt). Never returns secretKeyEnc or
      webhookTokenEnc to client.
    - `upsert` (writeProcedure): accepts {secretKey, publicKey, webhookToken, isLive,
      enabledMethods}; encrypts secretKey + webhookToken via @/lib/crypto.encrypt;
      upserts TenantXenditConfig row scoped to ctx.tenantId; sets isVerified=false
      (forces re-test after any credential change).
    - `testConnection` (writeProcedure): looks up config, decrypts secret, creates a
      tiny $0.01 invoice on Xendit's API with externalId=`test-${tenantId}-${nonce}`,
      immediately voids it via Xendit's expireInvoice endpoint, on success flips
      isVerified=true. On failure: leaves isVerified=false, returns error message.
    - `delete` (writeProcedure): removes the config row entirely (tenant going off
      Xendit). Throws if any EcommerceOrder.xenditPaymentId references would dangle.
- MOD: `apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/_app.ts` — register adminXenditConfig router.
- NEW: `apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/settings/xendit/page.tsx` — Server shell.
- NEW: `apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/settings/xendit/config-form.tsx` — Client
  form with masked-display for secret/webhook fields (show ••••••••, edit button reveals
  empty input for replacement). "Test connection" button calls testConnection procedure.
  Status badge: isVerified ✅ vs ⚠ unverified.
- NEW: `apps/web/src/__tests__/admin-xendit-config.test.ts` — coverage:
    - upsert encrypts secretKey + webhookToken (verify ciphertext is NOT plaintext via
      decrypt roundtrip in test)
    - get never returns secretKeyEnc or webhookTokenEnc fields
    - upsert resets isVerified to false
    - testConnection happy path (mocked Xendit createInvoice + expireInvoice succeed)
      flips isVerified to true
    - testConnection failure (mocked Xendit createInvoice throws) leaves isVerified
      false + returns error message
    - delete blocked when referenced by existing EcommerceOrder.xenditPaymentId
    - non-admin role rejection
    - cross-tenant isolation (admin from tenant A cannot read/write tenant B config)
- NO MIGRATION — TenantXenditConfig already exists in init migration (schema.prisma
  line 160). Schema pre-flight item 5 will pay off 9th consecutive batch.

Branch: feat/batch-21b-xendit-config-admin
RED→GREEN: write 8 procedure tests first, confirm RED, then router + UI.

⚠ Pre-flight specifics for this batch:
- Verify `_app.ts` (root tRPC router file) location and naming convention by grepping
  for storefrontRouter registration.
- Verify how existing "Tenant Administrator" role check is done (read storefront.ts
  requireAdmin helper for pattern).
- Verify which Xendit API methods are needed for testConnection — `Invoice.createInvoice`
  is known from Batch 17, but `Invoice.expireInvoice` (the void method) needs to be
  confirmed in xendit-node v7 SDK type definitions.
- Verify admin layout exists at /[slug]/(app)/settings or if a settings layout needs to
  be created. If absent: in-scope minimal settings index page that links to xendit
  subpage.
- masked-display pattern for sensitive fields: store the encrypted value server-side,
  return only "has-value: true/false" boolean to client. Form posts NEW values for
  replacement; never sends the existing encrypted value back.

## Alternative directions (pick instead if 21b feels too heavy)

- **Batch 21c (out of order)** — Refactor xendit.ts + webhooks/route.ts to use
  per-tenant config WITHOUT building the admin UI. Use a CLI seed script for now to
  populate TenantXenditConfig. T2 ~18K. Trade-off: humans can't manage Xendit creds
  via UI until 21b ships later.
- **Direction C** — Xendit prod-readiness bundle (Turnstile activation + webhook
  replay protection + Komodo Stack config). T2 ~25K. Independent of Direction F chain.
- **Direction D** — Small carry-forward bundle (guest order tracking page + audit-log
  for guest checkout + admin filter). T1 ~12K. Quick win.
- **Direction B** — Mobile Expo scaffold. T3 ~50K multi-session. Different track.

## Standing 9-point pre-flight (run before any code on any batch)

1. `git status` + `git log -1` — confirm tree state.
2. `pnpm vitest run` — confirm 706/706 GREEN baseline.
3. Read input Zod schema of any router procedure the batch claims to reuse.
4. If router newly READS a field, verify all existing tests on that path mock the field.
5. Grep schema.prisma for any model in scope; confirm fields before scoping migrations.
6. Confirm package.json has any third-party library called out in scope.
7. Re-read .claude/rules/memory-governance.md §1 for the tier classification.
8. Emit explicit branch-creation line item in the BUILD BATCH PROPOSAL.
9. For publicProcedure vs protectedProcedure claims, grep the router to verify.

## Recurring-pattern lessons banked (apply at next batch PRE-FLIGHT)

- 🟢 publicProcedure tenant resolution — input.tenantSlug → db.tenant.findUnique;
  default warehouse server-side. NEVER let client supply warehouseId on public path.
- 🟢 System-actor lookup for guest writes — db.user.findFirst({isActive:true},
  orderBy:{createdAt:"asc"}) returns seeded webmaster for required createdById FKs.
- 🟢 Rate-limit tier — rateLimiters.public.check(ip) at 10/min/IP for guest mutations
  (NOT 30/min — actual config is 10).
- 🟢 sanitizePlainText on user-facing text fields before storage.
- ⚖️ Order-creation duplication tolerated — extraction deferred until 3rd variant.
- 🔴 useCart() shape gotcha — destructure mismatch caught at typecheck.
- 🟢 Intentional scope-trim — 4× consecutive (cart-only, order-only, Xendit-only,
  crypto-only). Direction F NOW split 3 ways.
- 🟢 Helper-extract refactor pattern — protected→public dual-caller surfaces extract
  to src/lib/ helper.
- 🟢 RED-phase Zod-enum tightening — assert specific mock-side error marker + mock
  was-called to force true RED when new enum value would also Zod-reject.
- 🟢 Atomicity through in-transaction external calls — external HTTP inside DB
  transaction acceptable for payment surfaces.
- 🟢 As-any cast cleanup post-GREEN — grep `as any` after implementation; remove dead
  casts before lint flags them.
- 🟢 BUILT-IN NODE:CRYPTO SUFFICES — no need to add libsodium/tweetnacl for symmetric
  encryption. node:crypto + aes-256-gcm is FIPS-approved AEAD.
- 🟢 AES-256-GCM FORMAT — `{iv}.{authTag}.{ciphertext}` dot-separated base64url. IV
  12B per encryption (never reused), auth tag 16B mandatory.
- 🟢 LAZY ENV READ FOR TESTABILITY — getKey() reads process.env at CALL time, not
  module-import time. Tests manipulate env var per-test without vi.mock.
- 🟢 FILE-LEVEL RED — when test file imports not-yet-created module, vitest fails
  entire file at load. Still valid RED.
- 🟢 .env.example does NOT exist in this project. Skip it in future batches. Use
  .env.dev for runtime + CREDENTIALS.md for human-readable documentation.

## 🔴 CRITICAL — STAGING/PROD KEY DEPLOYMENT (before any 21b/21c deploy)

Before ANY batch that consumes @/lib/crypto can ship to staging or production:
1. Generate fresh APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY on each target server:
   `openssl rand -base64 32`
2. Add to .env.staging AND .env.prod (different value per env — never reuse across envs).
3. Document in CREDENTIALS.md (gitignored — agent writes, never reads back).
4. Komodo Stack: restart to pick up new env var.
5. Without these steps: env.ts validation fails at boot, app refuses to start.

Currently APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY exists ONLY in .env.dev. Staging/prod will boot-fail
the moment a batch using crypto is deployed.

